  "description": "Airborne radar pass NOAA42-20270914-0830Z, about 2,400 square km centred on Corpus Christi Bay at 5 m resolution, two and a half hours after landfall. Two large hulls alongside at the crude oil berth on the north bank of the Main Turning Basin in the Inner Harbor; no vessel under way anywhere in the ship channel. Storm-surge inundation of 2.1 to 3.4 m across the coastal industrial zone. Low-backscatter (oil-on-water) signature in the Inner Harbor around the berth, trailing east toward the bay.",
